# Shaded-jar mapping (requirement 37 of
# dev-support/licenses/License-Management.md).
#
# When a shipping jar relocates and embeds other artifacts, the archive's
# view (one jar) wins over the graph's view (several GAVs) for completeness
# checks; the embedded artifacts' licenses still apply and their texts stay
# in the resolved set. This file records which coordinates are embedded in
# which top-level jar, so check-archive-licenses.sh can annotate
# inventory entries that have no standalone jar in the archive.
#
# Format: `g:a # embedded in <top-level jar> — justification`
# Lines starting with # are comments and do not count as mappings.
#
# Grounded in the first ground-truth runs (42374519973/42380708044,
# 2026-11-07; record: 2026-11-07-1430-Archive-Ground-Truth-First-Run.md):
# - hadoop-gcp does NOT shade anything: its jar carries only its own
#   com/google/cloud/hadoop and org/apache/hadoop/fs classes (verified by
#   package listing) — the earlier "shaded google-cloud into hadoop-gcp"
#   premise was wrong; those coordinates ship as dependencies of the
#   cloud-storage dist (gated with the -Dhadoop-*-package flags).
# - hadoop-client-runtime relocates protobuf into
#   org.apache.hadoop.thirdparty.protobuf (embedded
#   hadoop-shaded-protobuf_3_25 pom.properties) and embeds a large set of
#   unrelocated runtime deps (jline, jetty, avro, jackson, gson,
#   nimbus, dnsjava, jsch, ...) whose standalone jars still ship for the
#   modules that need them. Correction 2026-11-09 (run 42543652715
#   worklist curation): kerby is only PARTLY embedded — the auth-chain
#   jars kerb-core/kerb-util/kerb-crypto/kerby-asn1/kerby-pkix ship
#   standalone; the kerby artifacts pulled only by hadoop-minikdc and
#   hadoop-client-minicluster (kerb-admin/client/common/identity/server/
#   simplekdc, kerby-xdr, token-provider) are NOT in the runtime shade
#   set and exist nowhere in the archive — they are curated out of the
#   inventory via the root pom's excludedArtifacts, not listed here.

com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java # embedded in hadoop-client-runtime — shaded/relocated to org.apache.hadoop.thirdparty.protobuf via hadoop-shaded-protobuf_3_25 (embedded pom.properties evidence)
com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java-util # embedded in hadoop-client-runtime — shaded/relocated with protobuf-java
io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-common # embedded in hadoop-gcp — shaded/relocated to com.google.cloud.hadoop.repackaged.ossgcs.io.opentelemetry (upstream pom: opentelemetry-bom 1.59.0 import + io.opentelemetry.** shade include; the inventory resolves 1.59.0 only through hadoop-gcp's graph, and no standalone 1.59.0 jar ships)
